e is a retelling of  the opening moments of the original  destiny game  in the cosmodrome on earth this is a  much more condensed and easy to  understand  narrative a guardian rises simplifies  the law without adding too much extra  baggage for new players  this version of the story revolves  around shaw han who is attempting to  find his crew and get back to the tower  before disaster strikes it only takes a  few hours to complete and  explains how weapon types work lost  sectors patrols  it teaches all the basic elements that  make up the experience of destiny 2.  so if you've had a break definitely try  there first  destiny 2 beyond light adds a new  location to the game  europa europa the smallest of four moons  circling jupiter and if you look closely  enough you may spot jupiter in the sky  okay it's a little closer than i  expected europa is a frozen land  seemingly untouched for generations but  actually there's more going on here than  meets the eye  and an evil kell named eremus is  harnessing the power of darkness  in the hopes of making the fallen great  again in terms of law the big golf ball  used to look after the fallen but the  traveller left them in the past  and the fallen aren't too happy about  that in the past we've had to level up  to be able to play these expansions but  not this time around so if you're  worried about jumping back in after all  this time don't worry  all your characters will automatically  be upgraded to power level 1050  allowing you to get straight into the  new stuff instead of grinding levels to  play what you paid for  so fill your boots during the story we  will harness power of darkness  the sworn enemy of light in order to be  strong enough to take down eremus  and this signals the first new element  in destiny since  2014 six whole years we've had solar  void and dark ways to control our light  but now we can harness stasis a kind of  dark ice subclass  with some pretty impressive abilities my  hunter throws down a 