ged on console here  let me show you why this is a big deal  the typical default field of view is  usually stuck at around 75 degrees in  first person shooters  this gives us a blend of accuracy in  gunfights and enough peripheral vision  around the sides  to spot other threats any smaller than  this and people can get  motion sick and any wider than this  hitting shots becomes particularly  hard at range so 75 degrees became the  best  middle ground destiny 2 allows us to  change this on the fly  which means if you have a preference in  other games it can now be transferred  over  and fyi i much prefer 90 a heck of a lot  more visual space  without too much of a drop in accuracy  for the ultra competitive  destiny 2 now supports 120 frames per  second  in pvp matches the crucible the place  where you take on other guardians  is where your reactions and accuracy are  most needed  so 120 frames of smoothness gives you a  significant advantage over players stuck  on 30 frames per second this is usually  one of the key reasons why players  migrate to pc  to control frame rate and field of view  and overall be in charge of how their  game  looks and you guess what i'm gonna say  next all those options are now here  on next gen consoles we can now clean up  the image  however we want it to look and finally  for next generation updates  the boot up times the loading speed is  now mind-blowing  the solid-state drives offer near  instant loading into and out of  encounters  and the same goes for character updates  of course we've still got to fly to our  destinations that will always take time  in an online game  but for context i used to watch players  speed running raids  back in the day and one of those people  was tfu and i always remember him saying  the hardest thing in speedrunning was  switching  your character's abilities around while  you waited for them to update  on ps5 and xbox series x this issue  is no more so there we have it a bunch  of cool things in the latest version of  destiny 2  beyond light from technical improvements  on console to a brand new adventure  which will make up a new trilogy in  years to come  now looks like a good time to try  destiny 2 completely free  and if you like the core loop of  shooting and looting you may want to try  the expansion beyond light  there is far more to look at and the  more i play destiny the more i want to  play destiny  so if you'd like me to cover this in  future just let me know you're in charge  of the future of this channel  i'm adam from playstation grenade thanks  to bungie for inviting me back to the  world of destiny 2 and for sponsoring  this video  it's been a pleasure i'll see you next  [Music]  time  you

